          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Hochschild (co)homology is a homological construction which makes sense for any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectrum"} ring spectrum
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            %em commutative
            algebras; an exposition of the noncommutative case remains to be written.
          %p
            Thus, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            a commutative
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-algebra"} ∞-algebra
            %em Hochschild homology complex
            is its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimit"} (∞,1)-tensoring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1 \cdot A
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            incarnation of the circle. More generally, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            any
            = succeed "-groupoid/simplicial" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \cdot A
            is the corresponding
            %em higher order Hochschild homology
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            In the presence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+algebras+on+%E2%88%9E-stacks"} function algebras on ∞-stacks
            it may happen that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = \mathcal{O}(X)
            is the algebra of functions on some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(-)
            sends
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/powering"} powering
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to tensorings of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(X)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(X)
            is the function complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(\mathcal{L}(X))
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+loop+space"} derived loop space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}X
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h3#TraditionalIdeas The Hochschild complex
          %p
            Originally the notion of Hochschild homology was introduced as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+homology"} chain homology
            of a certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            associated to any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimodule"} bimodule
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            over some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bar+complex"} bar complex
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi N
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mi op
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} B
                    %mo •
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C_\bullet(A,N)
                  \\coloneqq
                  N \otimes_{A \otimes A^{op}} \mathrm{B}_\bullet A
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            are regarded as
            = succeed "-bimodules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \otimes A^{op}
          %p
            Then it was understood that this complex is the result of tensoring the
            = succeed "-bimodules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \otimes A^{op}
            but using the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            functor – the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tor+functor"} Tor functor
            – in the ambient
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+chain+complexes"} model structure on chain complexes
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi N
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mi op
                    %mi D
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Tor
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mi op
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi N
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C_\bullet(A,N) = N \otimes^D_{A\otimes A^{op}} A = Tor^\bullet_{A\otimes A^{op}}(N,A)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Then still a little later, it was understood that this is just the ordinary tensor product in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal (∞,1)-category
            of
            = succeed "es." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi N
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mi op
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C_\bullet(A,N)
                  \\coloneqq
                  N \otimes_{A \otimes A^{op}} A
                  \\,.
          %p
            This, generally, is the definition of the Hochschild homology object of any bimodule over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+in+a+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} monoid
            in a symmetric monoidal
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{op}
            %em cohomology
            object is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C^\bullet(A,N)
                  \\coloneqq
                  Hom_{A\otimes A^{op}}(A,N).
          %p
            Of special interest is the case where
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N = A
            = succeed "-\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %strong center
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Z(A)
                  \\coloneqq
                  Hom_{A\otimes A^{op}}(A,A).
          %p
            Dually, the Hochschild homology object when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo =
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N=A
            is called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+trace"} universal trace
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %em shadow
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = \mathcal{O}(X)
            can be identified with an
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi op
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{op}= A
            = succeed "-pullbacks," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Z(\mathcal{O}(X)) \simeq \mathcal{O}(X \times_{X \times X} X)
                  \\simeq
                  \\mathcal{O}(\mathcal{L}X)
          %p
            is the
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+loop+space+object"} free loop space object
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h3#properties Properties
          %p
            By the
            %a{:href => "#HochschildKostantRosenberg"} Hochschild-Kostant-Rosenberg theorem
            and its generalizations, the Hochschild homology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi HH
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} HH_\bullet(\mathcal{O}(X),\mathcal{O}(X))
            of an ordinary algebra tends to behave like the algebra of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+differentials"} Kähler differentials
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(X)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotangent+complex"} cotangent complex
            of the
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(X)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cup+product"} cup product
            gives the wedge product of forms and the
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
          %p
            Dually this means that in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+geometry"} derived geometry
            the free loop space object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L} X
            consists of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+object"} infinitesimal
            loops in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (in ordinary geometry it would be equal to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec A
          %p
            Analogously, Hochschild
            %em cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi HH
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} HH^\bullet(\mathcal{O}(X), \mathcal{O}(X))
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(X)
            computes the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multivector+field"} multivector field
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(X)
            is a noncommutative algebra.
          %h2#Details Definition
          %p We start with the general-abstract definition of Hochschild homology and then look at special and more traditional cases.
          %h3#GeneralAbstractDefinition General abstract
          %p We look at the very general abstract definition of Hochschild (co)homology and some important subcases.
          %h4#hochschild_homology Hochschild homology
          %p We discuss Hochschild homology of commutative algebras for the case that these are related to function algebras on derived loop spaces.
          #DefByTensoring.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              that admits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+algebras+on+%E2%88%9E-stacks"} function algebras on ∞-stacks
              (see there for details)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi op
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi 𝒪
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Alg^{op} \stackrel{\overset{\mathcal{O}}{\longleftarrow}}{\underset{}{\longrightarrow}}
                    \\mathbf{H}
                    \\,.
            %p
              In particular the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-algebra"} ∞-algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg^{op}
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimit"} (∞,1)-tensored
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Alg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in Alg
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ∈
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \in \infty Grpd
              we say that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Alg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    K \cdot A \in Alg
            %p
              is the
              %em Hochschild homology complex
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %p
              We say a full
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} sub-(∞,1)-category
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              consists of
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒪
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
                \-perfect objects
              if on these
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
              commutes with
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limit"} (∞,1)-limit
            %p
              Then for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              an
              = succeed "-perfect" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒪
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    K \cdot \mathcal{O}(X)
                    \\simeq
                    \\mathcal{O}(X^{K})
                    \\,.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K = S^1
            the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
            %em ordinary
            Hochschild homology, while for general
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            it is called
            %em higher order Hochschild homology
            \.
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
              the functor that forms
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal (∞,1)-categories
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+sheaf"} quasicoherent ∞-stacks of modules
              over
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-site"} (∞,1)-site
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-algebra+over+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-algebraic+theory"} ∞-algebras
              for the ordinary theory of commutative
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Ben-ZviFrancisNadler"} Ben-ZviFrancisNadler
          %p
            The following definition formalizes large classes of
            = succeed "-perfect" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representables
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-algebraic+theory"} (∞,1)-algebraic theory
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg_\infty
              its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              of
              = succeed "-algebras." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi C
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi T
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Alg
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \hookrightarrow C \hookrightarrow T Alg_\infty^{op}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} small
              full
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} sub-(∞,1)-category
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Alg
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg_\infty^{op}
              which is closed under
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limit"} (∞,1)-limit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi Alg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg
              and equipped with the structure of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcanonical+coverage"} subcanonical
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-site"} (∞,1)-site
            %p
              Take
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} \coloneqq Sh(C)
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+geometry"} derived geometry
              modeled on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %msub
                        %mi Alg
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg_\infty
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ↪
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \hookrightarrow \mathbf{H}
              for the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Yoneda+embedding"} (∞,1)-Yoneda embedding
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in C\stackrel{}{\hookrightarrow} \mathbf{H}
              write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(X)
              for the same object regarded as an object of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %msub
                        %mi Alg
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg_\infty
          .num_defn
            %h6#propositiondefinition Proposition/Definition
            %p In the context of the above definition we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mn ∞
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{O} (\mathcal{L}X) \simeq S^1 \cdot \mathcal{O}(X) \in T Alg_\infty
                    \\,,
            %p
              where on the right we have the
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/limit+in+a+quasi-category#Tensoring"} (∞,1)-tensoring
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg_\infty
              over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi Grpd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty Grpd
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimit"} (∞,1)-colimit
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
              constant on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(X)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S^1 \cdot \mathcal{O}(X) \simeq {\lim_{\to}}_{S^1} \mathcal{O}(X)
                    \\,.
            %p
              This object we call the
              %strong Hochschild homology complex
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}X
            %p Generally for higher order Hochschild homology we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mi K
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mn ∞
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{O}(X^K) \simeq K \cdot \mathcal{O}(X)
                    \\simeq
                    {\lim_{\to}}_{K} \mathcal{O}(X)
                    \\in T Alg_\infty
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Because the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Yoneda+embedding"} (∞,1)-Yoneda embedding
              preserves
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limits"} (∞,1)-limits
              the limit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^K
              may be computed in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is closed under limits in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Alg
                        %mn ∞
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg_\infty^{op}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^K
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %msup
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg^{op}
              is the colimit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \cdot \mathcal{O}(X)
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} opposite (∞,1)-category
              of
              = succeed "-algebras." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            This definition of general higher order Hochschild homology by
            = succeed "-copowering" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                explicit in
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#ToenVezzosi"} ToënVezzosi
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K = S^1
            %li
              %p
                almost explicit in (
                %a{:href => "#GinotTradlerZeinalian"}> GinotTradlerZeinalian
                ), for higher order Hochschild homology for
                = succeed "s." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
                %a{:href => "#OvercdgAlgs"} Higher order Hochschild homology modeled on cdg-algebras
            %li
              %p
                explicit in
                %a{:href => "#Ben-ZviFrancisNadler"} Ben-Zvi/Francis/Nadler, corollary 4.12
                for HH with values in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+sheaf"} quasicoherent ∞-stacks
                and over perfect
                = succeed "-stacks" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %h4#TopologicalChiralHomology Topological chiral homology
          %p
            Notice that the tensoring that gives the Hochschild homology is given by the
            = succeed "-colimit" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi A
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo →
                    %mi K
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  K \cdot A \simeq {\lim_\to}_K A
                  \\,.
          %p
            This generalizes to
            = succeed "-colimits" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            diagram.
          %p
            Specifically let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be framed
            = succeed "-manifold," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/little+k-cubes+operad"} En-algebra
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_X
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            whose objects are framed embeddings of disjoint unions of open discs into
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and morphisms are inclusions of these. Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_A
            be the functor that assigns
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{k}
            to an object corresponding to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            discs in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            Then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimit"} (∞,1)-colimit
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  {\lim_\to}_{D_X} F_A
          %p
            is called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+chiral+homology"} topological chiral homology
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            an ordinary associatve algebra, hence in particular an
            = succeed "-algebra," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            the circle, this reproduces the ordinary Hochschild homology of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            (see below).
          %p
            For more details see (
            %a{:href => "#GinotTradlerZeinalian"}> GinotTradlerZeinalian
            ).
          %h3#specific_concrete Specific concrete
          %p We unwind the above general abstract definition in special classes of examples and find more explicit and more traditional definitions of Hochschild homology.
          %h4#PirashviliHigherOrder Pirashvili’s higher order Hochschild homology
          %p
            We demonstrate how the above
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Pirashvili"} Pirashvili
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
              regarded as a 0-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncated"} truncated
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-algebraic+theory"} (∞,1)-algebraic theory
            %p
              Consider a
              = succeed "/on" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+T-algebras"} model structure on simplicial T-algebras
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+T-algebras"} homotopy T-algebras
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presenting
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg_\infty
              such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  it is a
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensoring"} tensoring
                  with simplicial sets preserves weak equivalences and hence cofibrant replacement.
            %p
              Then for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi T
                    %mi Alg
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(X) \in T Alg \hookrightarrow T Alg_\infty
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ∈
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \in \infty Grpd
              the higher order Hochschild homology complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \cdot \mathcal{O}(X)
              is presented by the ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensoring"} tensoring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \cdot \mathcal{O}(X)
              in the model category, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              incarnation of the
              = succeed "-groupoid." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              The
              = succeed "-tensoring" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presented
              by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
              is modeled by the ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensoring"} tensoring
              of the latter on a cofibrant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution"} resolution
              of the given object. This is discussed in the section
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/limit+in+a+quasi-category#ModelsForTensoring"} ∞-tensoring – models
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              We can always use the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+homotopy+T-algebras"} model structure on homotopy T-algebras
              to satisfy the assumption of the above proposition. That is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
              for every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              and every ordinary algebra is cofibrant in this structure.
            %p
              Notice that in this model category even if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(X)
              is fibrant (which it is if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}X
              is an ordinary algebra), then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \cdot \mathcal{O}(X)
              is in general far from being fibant. Computing the
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+homotopy+group"} simplicial homotopy group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \cdot \mathcal{O}(X)
              and hence the Hochschild homology involves passing to a fibrant reolsution of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \cdot \mathcal{O}(X)
              first, that will make it a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+T-algebra"} homotopy T-algebra
            %p
              On the other hand, if we find a simplicial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+T-algebras"} model structure on simplicial T-algebras
              (which are degreewise genuine
              = succeed "-algebras)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \cdot \mathcal{O}(X)
              will be
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+products+of+algebras"} tensor products of algebras
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \cdot \mathcal{O}(X)
              yields explicitly (under the
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            %p
              This is the case for the tensoring of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
              = succeed "\u2018s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Teimuraz+Pirashvili"} Teimuraz Pirashvili
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Pirashvili"} Pirashvili
            %p This we describe below
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  for ordinary Hochschild homology in
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a{:href => "#TensoringWithSimplicialCircleAlgebra"} Examples – Simplicial algebra on the circle
              %li
                %p
                  for higher order Hochschild homology of dg-algebras in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a{:href => "#OvercdgAlgs"} Higher order Hochschild homology modeled on cdg-algebras
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            We first give a detailed discussion of the standard Hochschild complex of a commutative algebra, but from the general abstract
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            Then we look in detail at higher order Hochschild homology in the
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-site"} (∞,1)-site
            of formal duals of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            %a{:href => "#JonesTheorem"} theorem by Jones
            on Hochschild homology and loop space cohomology is a natural consequence of the general machinery.
          %h3#GradingsAndConventions Gradings and conventions
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+geometry"} derived geometry
            two categorical gradings interact: a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive
            = succeed "-groupoid" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            has a space of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-morphism"} k-morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_k
            for all non-negative
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+T-algebra"} simplicial T-algebra
            of functions with a component in each non-positive degree. But the directions of the face maps are opposite. We recall the grading situation from
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+algebras+on+%E2%88%9E-stacks"} function algebras on ∞-stacks
          %p
            Functions on a bare
            = succeed "-groupoid" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+algebra"} cosimplicial algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
