          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              %strong (automorphisms of the odd line)
            %p
              This means that under the identification of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi k
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{B}\mathbb{Z}) \cdot k \simeq C^\infty(k^{0|1})
              with functions on the
              = succeed ",in" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/odd+line"} odd line
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi θ
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi θ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta \partial/\partial \theta
              on the odd line, and in degree 1 to the odd vector field
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∂
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo ∂
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} that
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial/\partial\that
            %p (…)
          %h4#ExplicitHochschildChains Traditional description of the Hochschild complex
          %p
            We spell out explicitly the Hochschild chain complex for an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
            (over some ring
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimodule"} bimodule
          #PlainBarComplex.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bar+complex"} bar complex
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connective+chain+complex"} connective
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} B
                      %mo •
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi k
                        %mi n
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ∂
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi k
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ∂
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathrm{B}_\bullet A \coloneqq
                    (
                    \\cdots \to A^{\otimes_k n}
                    \\stackrel{\partial}{\to}
                    A^{\otimes_k n-1}
                    \\to \cdots
                    \\to A \otimes_k A \otimes_k A
                    \\stackrel{\partial}{\to}
                    A \otimes_k A
                    )
            %p
              which in degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              has the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+power"} tensor power
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              with itself, and whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
              is given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 3
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\partial(a_0, a_1, \cdots a_n)
                    \\coloneqq
                    (a_0 a_1, a_2, \cdots, a_n)
                    \-
                    (a_0, a_1 a_2 , a_3, \cdots, a_n)
                    +
                    \\cdots
                    \- (-1)^n (a_0, a_1, \cdots, a_{n-1} a_n)
                    \\,,
            %p
              regarded as a chain complex in
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimodule"} bimodule
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              be an
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimodule"} bimodule
              %strong Hochschild chain complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\bullet(A,N)
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              with coefficients in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              is the chain complex obtained by taking in the
              %a{:href => "#PlainBarComplex"} bar complex
              degreewise the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              of
              = succeed "-bimodules" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ⊗
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mi op
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} B
                      %mo •
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C_\bullet(A,N)
                    \\coloneqq
                    N_{A \otimes A^{op}}\mathrm{B}_\bullet A
                    \\,.
            %p
              The
              %strong Hochschild homology
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              with coefficients in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology"} homology
              of the Hochschild chain complex, written
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi HH
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    HH_n(A,N)
                    \\coloneqq
                    H_n( C_\bullet(A,N))
                    \\,.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p
              At the level of the underlying
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi k
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mi op
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi N
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi k
                        %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    N_{A \otimes_k A^{op}} A^{\otimes_k (n+2)}
                    \\simeq
                    N \otimes_k \otimes A^{\otimes_k n}
            %p given on elements by sending
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ν
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∼
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mi ν
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mi ν
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\nu, (a_0, a_1, \cdots, a_n, a_{n+1}))
                    \\sim
                    (a_{n+1} \nu a_{0}, (1, a_1, \cdots, a_n, 1))
                    \\mapsto
                    (a_{n+1} \nu a_0, a_1, \cdots, a_n)
                    \\,.
            %p
              The action of the differential in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\bullet(A,N)
              on elements of the latter form is then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ν
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ν
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ν
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 3
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ν
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mi ν
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\partial(\nu, a_1, \cdots, a_n)
                    \=
                    (\nu a_1, a_2, \cdots, a_n)
                    \-
                    (\nu, a_1 a_2, a_3, \cdots)
                    +
                    \\cdots
                    +
                    (-1)^n
                    (\nu , a_1, \cdots, a_{n-1} a_n)
                    \- (-1)^{n}
                    (a_n \nu, a_1, a_2, \cdots, a_{n-1})
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              In words this means that the Hochschild complex is obtained from the bar complex by “gluing the two ends of a sequence of elements of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              to a circle by a bimodule”.
            %p
              The fact that the circle appears here has in fact a deep significance: the Hochschild chain complex may be understood in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
              as encoding functions on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+loop+space+object"} free loop space object
              of whatever
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              behaves like being functions on.
          %h4#FuncsOnDerivedLoopSpace As function algebra on the derived loop space
          %p
            We give a formal derivation of the Hochschild complex of an ordinary commutative associative algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(X)
            as the function algebra on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+loop+space"} derived loop space
            object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}X
            in the context of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+geometry"} derived geometry
          %p
            So let now
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
            of ordiary commutative
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncated"} truncated
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-algebraic+theory"} (∞,1)-algebraic theory
          .num_defn
            %h6#proposition_7 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CAlg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CAlg(k)_\infty
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+over+a+Lawvere+theory"} ∞-algebras
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presented
              by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+T-algebras"} model structure on simplicial commutative k-algebras
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi CAlg
                        %mi k
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi op
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi proj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (CAlg_k^{\Delta^{op}})_{proj}
            %p
              This is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalent
              to the standard
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-algebras"} model structure on connected dg-chain algebras
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi CAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                    %mo ≃
                    %msubsup
                      %mi dgAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mo +
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (CAlg_k^{\Delta^{op}})_{proj}
                    \\simeq
                    dgAlg_k^+
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_7 Proof
            %p
              The first statement is discussed at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-algebraic+theory"} (∞,1)-algebraic theory
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+T-algebra"} homotopy T-algebra
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+Dold-Kan+correspondence"} monoidal Dold-Kan correspondence
          %p Let
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi C
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi T
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Alg
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  T \subset C \subset  T Alg_\infty^{op}
          %p
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcanonical+coverage"} subcanonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-site"} (∞,1)-site
            that is a full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} sub-(∞,1)-category
            of formal duals of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-algebras," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limit"} (∞,1)-limit
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Alg
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg_\infty^{op}
          %p Let
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{H} \coloneqq Sh_{(\infty,1)}(C)
          %p
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaf+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-sheaf (∞,1)-topos
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            Following the notation at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isbell+duality"} Isbell duality
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+algebras+on+%E2%88%9E-stacks"} function algebras on ∞-stacks
            we write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi T
                  %msub
                    %mi Alg
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(X) \in T Alg_\infty
            for an object that under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Yoneda+embedding"} (∞,1)-Yoneda embedding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi T
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Alg
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \hookrightarrow T Alg_\infty^{op} \to \mathbf{H}
            maps to an object called
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi T
                    %mi Alg
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(X) \in T Alg \hookrightarrow T Alg_\infty
              an ordinary
              = succeed "-algebra," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+loop+space+object"} free loop space object
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∶−
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{L}X \coloneq [S^1,X]
            %p
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              formed in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              is the
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+loop+space"} derived loop space
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_5 Remark
            %p
              The term
              %em derived
              is just to emphasize that we do not form the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+loop+space+object"} free loop space object
              in an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              of
              = succeed "-sheaves" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              inside the 1-category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Alg
                        %mi k
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg_k^{op}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+loop+space"} derived loop space
              instead has rich interesting structure.
            %p
              But if the ambient context of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
              over the genuine
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-site"} (∞,1)-site
              of formal duals to
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %em free loop space objects
              \. They are canonically given.
          #LimitInAlg.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_8 Proposition
            %p
              We have that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(\mathcal{L}X)
              is given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pushout"} (∞,1)-pushout
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi CAlg
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CAlg_\infty
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mi X
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{O}\mathcal{L}X \simeq \mathcal{O}(X) \coprod_{\mathcal{O}(X)\otimes \mathcal{O}(X) } \mathcal{O}(X)
            %p
              hence by the universal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocone"} cocone
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mi ℒ
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo ←
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ←
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathcal{O}\mathcal{L}X &amp;\leftarrow&amp;
                    \\mathcal{O}(X)
                    \\\
                    \\uparrow &amp;&amp; \uparrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathcal{O}(X) &amp;\leftarrow&amp; \mathcal{O}(X) \otimes \mathcal{O}(X)
                    }
          .proof
            %h6#proof_8 Proof
            %p
              Since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stackification"} ∞-stackification
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L : PSh_{(\infty,1)}(C) \to \mathbf{H}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+exact+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} left exact (∞,1)-functor
              and hence preserves finite
              = succeed "s," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limit"} (∞,1)-limit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}X
              may be computed in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-presheaves
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi PSh
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh_{(\infty,1)}(C)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Yoneda+embedding"} (∞,1)-Yoneda embedding
              preserves all
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limit"} (∞,1)-limit
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-site"} (∞,1)-site
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %msub
                        %mi Alg
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg_\infty
              = succeed "-pullback" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed "-pushout" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} opposite (∞,1)-category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %msub
                        %mi Alg
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg_\infty
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_9 Proposition
            %p
              The
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O} \mathcal{L}X
              of functions on the derived loop space of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is when modeled by a simplicial algebra in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi CAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CAlg_k^{\Delta^{op}}
              under the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+Dold-Kan+correspondence"} monoidal Dold-Kan correspondence
              equivalent to the Hochschild chain complex of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}X
              with coefficients in itself:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mi X
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{O} \mathcal{L}X \simeq C_\bullet(\mathcal{O}(X), \mathcal{O}(X))
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_9 Proof
            %p
              First observe that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi CAlg
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CAlg_k
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+commutative+algebras"} tensor product of commutative algebras
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mi B
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \coprod B = A \otimes_k B
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the discussion at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+T-algebra"} homotopy T-algebra
              we may model
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg_\infty
              by the
              %em injective
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi T
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^{op}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localized
              at the morphisms
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi l
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo →
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi k
                      %mo +
                      %mi l
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T[k] \otimes T[l] \to T[k+l]
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi T
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mrow
                          %mi inj
                          %mo ,
                          %mi prod
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [T, sSet]_{inj,prod}
            %p
              By the
              %a{:href => "#LimitInAlg"} above proposition
              we have that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}\mathcal{L}X
              is given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pushout"} homotopy pushout
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi inj
                        %mo ,
                        %mi prod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [T, sSet]_{inj,prod}
              of
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi X
                    %mo ←
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{O}X \leftarrow \mathcal{O}(X)\otimes_k \mathcal{O}(X) \to \mathcal{O}(X)
                    \\,,
            %p
              where both morphism are simple the product on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi CAlg
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(X) \in CAlg_k
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pushout"} homotopy pushout
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
              we have that this homotopy pushout is computed by an ordinary pushout once we pass to a weakly equivalent diagram in which one of the two morphism is a cofibration of simplicial algebras.
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo ←
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msub
                              %mo ⊗
                              %mi k
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} B
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo =
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo =
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo ≃
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo ←
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msub
                              %mo ⊗
                              %mi k
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathcal{O}X
                    \&amp;\leftarrow&amp;
                    \\mathcal{O}(X)\otimes_k \mathcal{O}(X) &amp;\hookrightarrow&amp; \mathrm{B} \mathcal{O}(X)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{=}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{=}} &amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\simeq}}
                    \\\
                    \\mathcal{O}X &amp;\leftarrow&amp;
                    \\mathcal{O}(X)\otimes_k \mathcal{O}(X) &amp;\to&amp; \mathcal{O}(X)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              It is sufficient to find a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution"} resolution
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} B
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{B} \mathcal{O}(X)
              in the global model structure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi inj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [T, sSet]_{inj}
              because left Bousfield localization strictly increases the class of weak equivalences, so that every gloabl weak equivalence is also a local weak equivalence.
            %p
              Since we are in the
              %em injective
              model structure this just means that this morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} B
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(X) \otimes_k \mathcal{O}(X) \to \mathrm{B} \mathcal{O}X
              needs to be over each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^n
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              of simplicial sets. If we find
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} B
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{B} \mathcal{O}X
              also as a strictly product-preserving functor (notice that the general functor in our model category need not even preserve products weakly, it will do so after fibrant replacement) then it being monomorphism over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^1
              implies that it is monic over every
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^n
            %p
              There is a standard resolution of the kind we need called the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bar+complex"} bar complex
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#Ginzburg"} Ginzburg, page 16
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
              in the category of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(X)
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
              to regard it as a simplicial module it is naturally even a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
              in
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi CAlg
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CAlg_k
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} B
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi k
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi k
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi k
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mover
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mi Id
                              %mo ⊗
                              %mi Id
                              %mo ⊗
                              %mi μ
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mi Id
                              %mo ⊗
                              %mi μ
                              %mi Id
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %mi μ
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi Id
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi Id
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi k
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi k
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %mi Id
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi μ
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %mi μ
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi Id
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi k
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mi CAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathrm{B} \mathcal{O}(X)
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\left(
                    \\cdots
                    \\mathcal{O}(X) \otimes_k \mathcal{O}(X) \otimes_k
                    \\mathcal{O}(X) \otimes_k \mathcal{O}(X)
                    \\stackrel{\overset{\mu \otimes Id \otimes Id}{\longrightarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{Id \otimes \mu Id}{\longrightarrow}}{\underset{Id \otimes Id \otimes \mu}{\longrightarrow}}}
                    \\mathcal{O}(X) \otimes_k \mathcal{O}(X) \otimes_k
                    \\mathcal{O}(X)
                    \\stackrel{\overset{\mu \otimes Id}{\longrightarrow}}{\underset{Id \otimes \mu}{\longrightarrow}}
                    \\mathcal{O}(X) \otimes_k \mathcal{O}(X)
                    \\right)
                    \\in
                    CAlg_k^{\Delta^{op}}
                    \\,,
            %p with the evident face and degeneracy maps given by binary product operation in the algebra and insertion of units.
            %p
              Take the morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} B
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(X) \otimes \mathcal{O}(X) \to \mathrm{B} \mathcal{O}(X)
              degreewise to be the inclusion of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(X) \otimes \mathcal{O}(X)
              as the two outer direct summands
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi Id
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi e
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi e
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi e
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi Id
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %mi ⋯
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{O}(X)
                    \\otimes_k
                    \\mathcal{O}(X)
                    \\stackrel{Id \otimes e \otimes e \otimes \cdots \otimes e \otimes Id}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\mathcal{O}(X) \otimes_k \mathcal{O}(X) \otimes_k \cdots
                    \\otimes_k \mathcal{O}(X)
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo :
                    %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e : k \to \mathcal{O}(X)
              is the monoid unit.
            %p
              This is clearly degreewise a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+complex"} Moore complex
              functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi Ab
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N : Ab^{\Delta^{op}} \to Ch_\bullet^+
              it maps to the standard bar complex resolution as found in the traditional literature (as reviewed for instance in
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Ginzburg"} Ginzburg
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology"} homology
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+homotopy+group"} simplicial homotopy group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology"} homology
              groups, we find that indeed
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mo :
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} B
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu : \mathrm{B}\mathcal{O}(X) \to \mathcal{O}(X)
              is a weak equivalence in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi inj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [T,sSet]_{inj}
              and hence in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi T
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mrow
                          %mi inj
                          %mo ,
                          %mi prod
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [T, sSet]_{inj,prod}
            %p
              We may now compute the pushout in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [T, sSet]
              and this will compute the desired homotopy pushout. Notice that this pushout indeed takes place just in simplicial copresheaves, not in product-preserving copresheaves!
            %p But this ordinary pushout it manifestly the claimed one.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_6 Remark
            %p This derivation
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  crucially uses the assumption that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
